From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peter Huang <peter.huang@ui.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 10:15:52 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] [cache] Fix unclean-shutdown dirty-bitset handling in
 cache_check and cache_dump

The cache target's on-disk dirty bitset is only written on a clean suspend.
After an unclean shutdown the kernel ignores it entirely and assumes every
mapped cache block is dirty, so the metadata legitimately contains dirty bits
for blocks that are no longer mapped. thin-provisioning-tools treated that
stale bit as a fatal inconsistency:

  * cache_check cross-checked the dirty bitset against the mapping tree and
    failed (exit 64) on a dirtied-but-unmapped block, so LVM refused to
    activate the cached LV and the machine was unbootable after a power loss;
  * cache_dump (and therefore cache_repair/cache_restore) copied those stale
    bits and wrote a superblock with clean_shutdown=1, so blocks dirtied after
    the last suspend came back marked clean and were never written back.

With this change both tools honour the kernel's rule when, and only when, the
superblock says the shutdown was not clean:

  * cache_check gains a check_dirty_bits flag on format2::MappingChecker, set
    from sb.flags.clean_shutdown, and skips the dirty-bit cross-check when the
    shutdown was unclean. A stale bit with clean_shutdown=1 is still fatal.
  * cache_dump computes all_dirty = !sb.flags.clean_shutdown and emits every
    mapping with dirty="true" for both the format1 and the format2 emitters,
    so a dump/restore round trip preserves the kernel's "everything is dirty"
    state instead of silently losing it.

Upstream: https://github.com/jthornber/thin-provisioning-tools/issues/330
Upstream fix: https://github.com/jthornber/thin-provisioning-tools/pull/331

This is a squash of the two commits of PR #331, rebased onto v1.3.4, where
they apply without conflict. Authorship is upstream's.

(cherry picked from commit 85b423e1177a271e603b54b73e732752d1bc9616)
(cherry picked from commit 7230adedeeef1df66b7865d476aed73607c1714e)
